<p>This is river country. The Paint Rock River and its tributaries have shaped the landscape, creating fertile bottomland that attracted settlers centuries ago. The homes here reflect that history — old farmhouses, historic structures, and the occasional newer build on family land.</p>

<p><strong>Valley drainage challenges:</strong> The valley acts like a funnel during heavy rain. Water flows down from the ridges on both sides, collecting in the valley floor. Properties here don't just deal with rain that falls directly on them — they manage water from a much larger drainage area. Gutters need to handle this volume without backing up.</p>

<p><strong>River humidity:</strong> Living near the river means elevated humidity year-round. This accelerates wood rot and corrosion, making gutter maintenance more critical. We often recommend aluminum gutters for valley properties because they resist rust better than steel alternatives.</p>

